<BaseLayout
  title={'What "read-only" means for a CloudOps Guard audit — CloudOps Guard'}
  description="CloudOps Guard reads supported metadata and configuration and never creates, patches, deletes, or remediates a resource -- and what it deliberately never collects."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="status-label status-label--neutral">Learn</p>
      <h1>What "read-only" means for a CloudOps Guard audit</h1>

      <p>
        CloudOps Guard reads the metadata and configuration its implemented checks need &mdash; for
        example, a Kubernetes container's declared resource requests/limits and image reference, or a
        GitLab project's protected-branch rules and CI/CD settings.
      </p>

      <p>
        It never creates, patches, deletes, or otherwise remediates a resource in the system it audits.
        Every check is read-only by construction: an audit run cannot change the cluster or project it
        looks at, regardless of what it finds.
      </p>

      <h2>What is not collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Kubernetes Secret or ConfigMap contents.</li>
        <li>Kubernetes container environment-variable values.</li>
        <li>Kubernetes application logs.</li>
        <li>GitLab CI/CD variables (CloudOps Guard never calls a CI/CD variables endpoint).</li>
        <li>GitLab job traces, logs, or artifacts.</li>
        <li>GitLab credentials or tokens.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What a report represents</h2>
      <p>
        A CloudOps Guard report contains the findings produced by the checks that are actually
        implemented today &mdash; it is not proof of comprehensive health, security, or compliance. The
        absence of a finding for a given check is not proof that check ran and passed; and there may be
        real issues no implemented check looks for yet. See the <a href="/checks">check catalogue</a> for
        exactly what is evaluated.
      </p>

      <p><a href="/learn">&larr; Back to Learn</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
